u_{r}(n)=\frac n2-1,\qquad u_{r}(n\pm1)=n\pm1-1
\end{equation*}
is satisfied for every even $n>0$ and the two odd neighbours lie on the
generic odd branch $u_{r}=n-1$.  Up to the free particle $n=2$,
$V\equiv0$, the first non-trivial even numbers are

\begin{equation*}
n_{1}=4\;,\qquad n_{2}=6\;,
\end{equation*}
the degenerate free convention being $n_{1}^{0}=2,\;n_{2}^{0}=4$.
